---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../data/site.js';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description={`How ${SITE_NAME} handles data.`} crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' }]}>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <p>The tools run in your browser. Numbers and dates you enter (MMSI, beacon IDs, certificate dates) are not sent to our server; they only appear in the page address if you choose to share a link.</p>
  <h2>Service requests</h2>
  <p>When you send a service request, we receive the details you provide: ship name and IMO number, port and dates, equipment and problem, your name, company, email and phone. We use them only to handle your request: we forward them to service partners covering the port so they can contact you with availability and a quote. We do not sell your data or use it for unrelated marketing.</p>
  <p>We keep requests as long as needed to handle them and for our records, and delete them on request. To access, correct or delete your data, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4, a service of Google Ireland Limited, to see in aggregate which pages are visited, how the tools are used and how many service requests are prepared. We do not use advertising cookies. Google may process this data outside your country, including in the United States.</p>
  <p>If you visit from Europe, Google Analytics does not load until you click "Accept" in the cookie notice. Elsewhere it runs with advertising storage switched off. You can change your choice at any time with the "Cookies" link at the bottom of each page.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td><td>Google Analytics: distinguish visits and sessions</td><td>Up to 2 years</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>fvt_consent</code></td><td>Remember your cookie choice (browser local storage)</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</Base>
